# What EAS Build uploads to its servers. Unlike .gitignore, this controls a
# real production build's inputs, not git history — and .easignore fully
# replaces .gitignore rather than adding to it, so everything useful from
# .gitignore has to be repeated here.
#
# The one deliberate difference: apps/mobile/assets/data/ is excluded from
# git (it's 77 MB+ of map data, refreshed daily, published via GitHub
# Releases rather than committed) but it is NOT excluded here, because the
# app statically `require()`s those files at bundle time. A production build
# that cannot see them fails immediately with "Unable to resolve module" —
# discovered by actually running a production build and reading the real
# EAS build log, not by reasoning about it in the abstract.

node_modules/

data/raw/
data/out/
data/basemap/

# Generated by `expo prebuild`; the config in app.json is the source of truth.
apps/*/ios/
apps/*/android/

.DS_Store
.expo/
dist/

# Apple/Google credential files. Referenced by path from eas.json (not
# secret); the files themselves must never leave this machine.
apps/mobile/secrets/

# The wildcards below would otherwise also match the staged data files this
# ignore file exists to include, so the negations at the end are load-
# bearing — .easignore follows gitignore syntax, where a later `!` pattern
# can re-include specific files even after a broader pattern excluded them,
# as long as the parent directory itself was never directory-excluded.
*.geojsonl
*.pmtiles
*.sqlite
!apps/mobile/assets/data/**
